---
interface Surface {
  name: string;
  commands: string;
}

interface Props {
  surfaces: Surface[];
}

const { surfaces } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="inventory-panel mt-11 border-t border-base-300 pt-6">
  <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">the generated command surface</span>
      <h3 class="mt-1 mb-0 text-[clamp(19px,2.2vw,24px)] leading-[1.2]">Every branch, still namespaced.</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="badge badge-secondary">14 APIs</span>
  </div>
  <div class="grid">
    {
      surfaces.map((surface) => (
        <details class="collapse collapse-arrow inventory-item rounded-none">
          <summary class="collapse-title min-h-12 px-1 text-sm">
            <span>{surface.name}</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="collapse-content px-1">
            <code>{surface.commands}</code>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="m-0 mt-3.5 max-w-[74ch] text-[13px] text-(--muted)">
    Run <code>grr &lt;service&gt; --help</code> and <code>grr schema</code> for the exact flags. The tree is generated from Google's Discovery Service - every method nests by resource (<code>grr gmail users messages list</code>, <code>grr drive files get</code>) with typed flags per parameter. <code>grr api list</code> and <code>grr api describe</code> are the flat, id-based equivalents.
  </p>
</div>
